ators on here  that i follow watching them get nuked by  teleporting or rubber banding enemies  man there is no world where that feels  good i'm gonna be straight with you i  have no idea how bad it can get on old  gen and how much of that seems to be a  combination of the hardware and the  state of battlefield 2042 servers what i  do know is there are going to be a lot  of pissed off players trying to upgrade  to next gen that can't and they're  pulling their hair out just to get a  full proper match going on their old gen  console when you drop 60 to 70 bucks on  a game the hope is that it actually  works and that just isn't always the  case from what we've seen in battlefield  2042's beta what's even more troubling  is that the clock is ticking 2042 comes  out on november 12th for early access  folks and that's a real tight deadline i  am all for being optimistic and hoping  for the best but there are some very  real issues here and if we're paying  that full price it's kind of our right  to expect something more complete than  what we've seen so far so optimization  is huge for old gen but general  bugginess and glitches need an extra  look even on current gen platforms  thankfully there have already been quite  a few changes to the gameplay based on  feedback but they're not particularly  groundbreaking they're still nice to  hear about though seriously for example  the removal of bunny hopping to exploit  speed boost or reduced vehicle animation  times these are nice changes and it's  also nice to know that we're getting  more tanks per orbital match with eight  total up from four but that is only on  next gen which also kind of underlines  my point these changes are addressing  the minor stuff and they don't really  address the more substantial issues for  the community playing on last gen not to  mention we need solutions that are more  convincing for other issues such as  specialists  reporting for duty yeah this is going to  be the meatiest part of the video  because there is a lot to unpack with  the new specialists that were revealed  and honestly trying to figure out  whether specialists will ever gel with  battlefield's identity it's that's tough  unfortunately i wonder if their  inclusion is one that we will have to  make peace with although it will not be  an easy sell many folks are  to put it lightly  not fans of specialists i mean shoot the  new specialist trailer has been getting  rationed on our channel already any  youtube video or twitch stream that you  watch has had increasingly vocal please  for something to be done about  specialists and dice has done something  kinda see now on the blog post it seems  like dice is convinced that the more  specialists that we have the less upset  the community will be which i'm not so  sure is true they mentioned that issues  with the ui recognizing friend or foe  and a poor ping system were issues  during the beta that most likely limited  us in experiencing specialists the way  that they were originally designed which  is fair and we'll get to that granular  quality of life update soon but i can  tell you right now that to me it wasn't  really the ui or the lack of in-game  comms that made specialists feel like  lone wolves you see specialists  unfortunately take away from the core  idea of a small soldier in a big war  that battlefield games have done so well  in the past we've never been apex legend  style heroes or overwatch characters  with backstories we've always just been  another soldier maybe with a particular  dog tag at first i didn't mind the  specialist really because i took  advantage of mckay's grapple hook and  his character abilities while ziplining  but i've definitely pivoted on the  subject for sure after hearing things  from your guys's point of view in the  comments still i also have more  experience playing other shooter games  so that hero aspect didn't feel foreign  to me but once i settled into my  thoughts a bit and i heard all of your  guys's comments it made more sense just  because that kind of hero style gameplay  is common in other shooters that does  not mean that it belongs in battlefield  alright let's break down how significant  these new specialists are supposed to be  and remember the idea is that with more  specialists we're supposed to have  better team play  i mean okay so on the assault side the  two new ones you have dozer and sundance  dozer looks built like a tank style roll  rather than an assault and has extra  resistance to explosives and a riot  shield to help push through choke points  by reflecting bullets sundance on the  other hand already sounds overpowered  she's the only specialist with the  wingsuit which means traversing through  air and even those tornadoes are going  to be a hell of a lot easier giving a  significant mobility advantage over the  other specialists what's making me raise  my eyebrows though are these smart  explosives not to mention letting anyone  play a sundance and equip whatever  loadout they want isn't even playing as  assault the specialists make the  original classes completely obsolete in  a way they literally even show her using  an lmg alongside different kinds of  smart explosives and just nothing makes  sense anymore i've mentioned in earlier  videos that battlefield is at its best  when there are two things chaotic  battlefield moments that you would only  see in hollywood type movies and a  balanced level of immersion battlefield  1 did this exceptionally well with its  first person animations whenever you  used field guns or clambered from seat  to c in the fighter plane those moments  were perfect in letting your regular  character feel like a maverick or a hero  while remaining unnamed without a padded  backstory specialists flip the script a  bit and haven't done it well from an  immersion standpoint especially when you  see a bunch of folks running around and  none of them actually you know healing  their team one positive note though is  that they have added extended time for  auto heal so you will be at the mercy of  faulk now on your squad more often which  will hopefully get the medics to focus  on heels a bit more speaking of folk and  the lack of medics there weren't any  other medic specialists though you had  the two assault specialists we mentioned  earlier and two new recon specialists in  rao and pake that basically had wall  hacks i'm not kidding rau's ability lets  you kill a hacked target to reveal  enemies in the immediate area which stay  with me here you have to see someone not  shoot them  take the time to hack them hoping that  they don't see you  and  that then you shoot them like it's not  that's not how shooters work  meanwhile pake would highlight anyone  that damaged you but also had an emg x  scanner that literally just showed  hostels in cover who needs pc hacks when  the game is basically giving them to  particular specialists as an occasional  freebie the odds that solo players are  going to load in and decide to gravitate  towards specialists that are overpowered  is extremely high to put it lightly that  does not bode well for trying to  encourage more team play i wasn't  entirely sure if her wall's ability  passes onto squadmates or teammates in  the vicinity because if it does then  yeah that would technically help team  play but that would also just be broken  as hell once again the gameplay as a  solo player is still fun but this is not  call of duty or overwatch it feels the  opposite of what a battlefield  experience should be which prioritizes  squad cooperation being a solo twitch  streamer that can rack up 70 plus elims  per game is great but in conquest it's  squads that make the fights feel  meaningful at the very least i would  like to see some kind of lockout so you  can only have one of each specialist per  squad so no double dipping now they have  confirmed that that lockout will be the  case for the recently announced hazard  zone at the very least 